DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
       ddppkkgg--ttrriiggggeerr is a tool to explicitly activate triggers and check for
       its support on the running ddppkkgg.

       This can be used by maintainer scripts in complex and conditional
       situations where the file triggers, or the declarative aaccttiivvaattee
       triggers control file directive, are insufficiently rich. It can also
       be used for testing and by system administrators (but note that the
       triggers won't actually be run by ddppkkgg--ttrriiggggeerr).

       Unrecognized trigger name syntaxes are an error for ddppkkgg--ttrriiggggeerr.

